Request Name

Production Data Query for Incident Analysis – Sentinel PACS Fields Validation

Project Overview

Execution of controlled SQL queries in the production database to validate whether specific fields originating from SWIFT PACS messages are correctly stored in the database and subsequently propagated to the Sentinel system. The objective is to support incident investigation and identify the stage in the processing flow where the data is missing or incorrectly populated.

Data Objective (General description of the purpose of the data)

The purpose of accessing the data is to validate the integrity and traceability of specific fields associated with SWIFT PACS messages that are expected to populate records used by the Sentinel system.

The queries will allow verification of:

Whether the fields are correctly persisted in the production database.

Whether the information received from PACS messages is stored as expected.

At which stage of the processing pipeline the data may be lost, altered, or not populated.

This analysis is strictly limited to troubleshooting an incident and determining the root cause of incorrect or missing data in Sentinel.

